# Session tooling (local only). Ignored by the repository itself, deliberately,
# rather than relying on any contributor's personal global gitignore: these
# directories hold machine-local paths and scratch artifacts, and this is a
# public repository where a single `git add -A` on a fresh clone would publish
# them permanently.
.remember/
.claude/
.superpowers/

# Local Compose overrides, for the same reason as the block above. Compose
# merges docker-compose.override.yml automatically, so it is where a machine's
# own resource limits, ports, and mounts end up — details about someone's
# hardware or network that do not belong in a public repository. Ignored here
# rather than in one clone's .git/info/exclude, because a local exclude
# protects exactly the machine it was typed on and no other.
docker-compose.override.yml
